topics.theoryContent:
elif (else-if) adds more branches. Python checks the conditions top to bottom and runs the FIRST block whose condition is True; the rest are skipped. If none match, else runs.

score = int(input("Enter your score: "))
if score >= 90:
    grade = "A"
elif score >= 75:
    grade = "B"
elif score >= 60:
    grade = "C"
else:
    grade = "D"
print("Grade:", grade)

Order matters: conditions are tested from top to bottom, and the first True one wins. Write the most specific condition first. A score of 95 hits the first branch and never reaches the others.

You can chain as many elifs as you need.

