topics.theoryContent:
A nested if is an if inside another if. It lets you ask a second question only when the first is already answered.

Use it when one check only matters after another passes.

age = 25
has_id = True
if age >= 18:
    if has_id:
        print("Entry allowed")
    else:
        print("ID required for entry")
else:
    print("Entry denied — underage")

Nesting is powerful but easy to overuse. When the logic is "several conditions must ALL hold", prefer combining them with and instead of deep nesting:

if age >= 18 and has_id:
    print("Entry allowed")

Rule of thumb: two levels of nesting is fine; three or more is usually a signal to restructure (combining conditions, or functions on Day 20).

