topics.theoryContent:
range(n) produces the numbers 0, 1, 2, …, n-1. It is the standard way to repeat something a fixed number of times:

for i in range(5):
    print(i)     # prints 0 1 2 3 4

range(start, stop) — count from start to stop-1:
for i in range(2, 6):
    print(i)     # prints 2 3 4 5

range(start, stop, step) — with a step:
for i in range(0, 10, 2):
    print(i)     # prints 0 2 4 6 8

range returns a special lazy object, not a list — it produces numbers one by one as the loop asks for them, so counting to a billion costs almost nothing in memory.

