counts = {}
for word in text.split():
    counts[word] = counts.get(word, 0) + 1
print(counts)    # {'apple': 2, 'banana': 1}

The word counter is the famous dict pattern: get returns 0 for a new word, +1 builds the count, and the assignment stores it back. Entire search and analytics systems are built on this one pattern.

