topics.theoryContent:
The same shorthand works for sets and dictionaries, and that gives you concise versions of everyday tasks.

SET comprehension — deduplicate while transforming:
words = ["a", "b", "a", "c"]
unique_len = {len(w) for w in words}
print(unique_len)    # {1} — the set holds only unique lengths

