topics.theoryContent:
Beyond __init__, a class can have any number of normal methods that use the object's data:

class Student:
    def __init__(self, name, marks):
        self.name = name
        self.marks = marks

    def average(self):
        return sum(self.marks) / len(self.marks)

    def passed(self):
