topics.theoryContent:
Put the parent class name in brackets after the child's name:

class Vehicle:
    def start(self):
        print("Vehicle started")

class Car(Vehicle):
    def honk(self):
        print("Beep!")

c = Car()
c.start()     # inherited from Vehicle
c.honk()      # defined on Car

The child automatically has every method and attribute of the parent, PLUS its own. This is called "is-a" inheritance: a Car IS-A Vehicle, so it can do everything a Vehicle can, and more.

You can chain deeper — Truck(Vehicle), Minivan(Car) — building a hierarchy. Keep it shallow and meaningful; a hierarchy that matches real categories is the goal, not a deep tower of classes.

