topics.theoryContent:
A GENERATOR is a function that produces a sequence of values one at a time, using yield instead of return:

def count_up_to(n):
    i = 1
    while i <= n:
        yield i
        i += 1

for num in count_up_to(3):
    print(num)     # 1 2 3

The difference from return: return ends the function and gives back one value. yield PAUSES the function, hands out one value, and remembers where it left off. The next call resumes right after the yield.

Calling a generator function does NOT run it — it returns a generator OBJECT. Values are produced only as the loop demands them.

