def slow_sum(n):
    return sum(range(n))

One subtlety: wrapping replaces the function, so the wrapped version loses the original's name and docstring. Fix that with functools.wraps, which copies the metadata onto the wrapper:

from functools import wraps

def timer(func):
    @wraps(func)
    def wrapped(*args, **kwargs):
        ...
        return result
    return wrapped

Use @wraps on every decorator you write for real code — debugging tools (help, name, docstrings) depend on it.

